Description: touchscreen coffee monitor for the Technivorm at B451
 brewcop is a Kivy touchscreen app that watches a Moccamaster/Technivorm
 coffee machine.  It auto-detects brewing from the boiler current (a
 Phidgets i-Snail clamp over a VINT hub), weighs the carafe on an
 Avery-Berkel serial scale, and publishes a "ready" event to MQTT so a
 downstream consumer can notify however it likes (Slack, signage, ...).
 .
 It runs as a single systemd service on a read-only-root Raspberry Pi OS
 Lite kiosk driving the 7" DSI touchscreen directly via SDL2 on DRM/KMS.
